<article class="env-lemma" id="37CF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/37CF">Lemma <span data-tag="37CF">5.5.4.17</span>.</a> Let $f: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be a presentable functor between presentable $\infty $-categories, and let $\calC ^0 \subseteq \calC $ be a strongly reflective subcategory. Let $f^{\ast }$ denote a right adjoint of $f$, and let $\calD ^{0} \subseteq \calD $ be the full subcategory spanned by those objects $D \in \calD $ such that $f^{\ast } D \in \calC ^0$. Then $\calD ^{0}$ is a strongly reflective subcategory of $\calD $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $S$ be a (small) set of morphisms of $\calC $ such that $\calC ^0$ is the full subcategory of $\calC $ spanned by the $S$-local objects. Then $\calD ^0$ is the full subcategory of $\calD $ spanned by the $f(S)$-local objects. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>